"The secret of the Seals is an Insight the Conclave restricts."
"Seals are the source of all mana in Davrar: they purify it and also generate it."
"On Solstice night a Seal opens and sends great magic toward the central sun; Seals power the sun."
"Seals also unlock wizardry; the making of mana and of wizardry form one cycle."
"Seals are made of mana, wizardry and a third force Nathan did not understand."
"Seals hold blank spots beyond wizardry that make mana from nothing."
"Seals seem to split mana and wizardry out of a cosmological background."
"Seals feel like real physical machines, not weightless magical constructs."
"A Seal's parts rotate and lock into orientations that set which type of mana it makes."
"A normal Seal makes neutral mana."
"A Seal's wizardry switch sets it to purify magic or to corrupt it."
"Outside the Solstice a Seal can be adjusted only through wizardry, and only by a powerful wizard."
"Corrupting a Seal is simple; the blight it breeds fights anyone trying to fix it."
"Corrupting one Seal subverts some share of all mana in Davrar."
"A repaired Seal slowly refills drained ambient mana and purifies land in a widening ring."
"The aether holds the apparatus of the Seals; a scoured aether refills from the local Seal."
"Kaelis calls blighted death Seals undead Seals."
"The blights were meant as challenges, dungeons for Questors to conquer."
"The same Davrar-unique power that makes the Seals seems to govern Questor resurrection."
"The Questor link to Davrar feels more fundamental even than the Seals."
"Questors could not hold so many Seals without Travel."
"Travel needs uncorrupted Seals nearest both ends of the journey."
"The first arcane blight was born of a mortal hacking the Seals with unrestrained Insight."
"The magic sustaining Gemore's continent is inside the Gemore Seal."
"Later, Nathan sensed the Seals' apparatus in the aether and believed he could reset a Seal."
"Years later Nathan chose not to flip the Gemore Seal to another setting."
"Years later Nathan purged the blighted Seal near Helmaris; its purify switch had been disconnected."
"Nathan's Magical Destruction could break Seals and drain a continent's magic; he swore not to."
"Stella feared breaking Seals could bring the Ending of Silence."
"Years later the Heirs swore an oath on the Gemore Seal to end the Endings."
"Years later a Questor got a Davrar box making them answerable for a remote Seal at Sansal."
